  "tagline": "Developer-friendly Rust search engine with typo tolerance and built-in hybrid semantic search.",
  "description": "Meilisearch is a single-binary search engine written in Rust that gives you instant, typo-tolerant search with sane defaults and almost no tuning. Its hybrid search lets you plug in embedders (OpenAI, Hugging Face, Ollama, REST) so documents are vectorized automatically and ranked alongside keyword matches, and it now ships conversational chat endpoints for RAG-style answers. The core is MIT-licensed, while newer enterprise features such as sharding sit under BUSL-1.1. It shines for site, app and e-commerce search up to tens of millions of documents; it is not built for log analytics or heavy aggregations.",
